### `feature/user/data/remote/UserApiService.kt`

```kotlin
package com.enterprise.mobile.feature.user.data.remote

import kotlinx.serialization.SerialName
import kotlinx.serialization.Serializable
import retrofit2.Response
import retrofit2.http.GET
import retrofit2.http.Path

@Serializable
data class UserNetworkDto(
    @SerialName("id") val id: String,
    @SerialName("full_name") val fullName: String,
    @SerialName("email") val email: String,
    @SerialName("is_vip") val isVip: Boolean,
)

interface UserApiService {
    @GET("v1/users/{userId}")
    suspend fun fetchProfile(@Path("userId") userId: String): Response<UserNetworkDto>
}
```

Required fields have no invented empty/default values. Kotlin serialization checks payload structure; additional identity/business validation happens before persistence. The example endpoint expects HTTP 200 with a profile body. The approved network layer owns base URL, authentication, timeouts, redirects, response limits, retry policy, and serialization configuration.

