### `feature/user/data/local/UserDao.kt`

```kotlin
package com.enterprise.mobile.feature.user.data.local

import androidx.room.Dao
import androidx.room.Query
import androidx.room.Upsert

@Dao
interface UserDao {
    @Query("""
        SELECT * FROM user_profiles
        WHERE account_id = :accountId AND user_id = :userId
        LIMIT 1
    """)
    suspend fun find(accountId: String, userId: String): UserEntity?

    @Upsert
    suspend fun upsert(entity: UserEntity)

    @Query("""
        DELETE FROM user_profiles
        WHERE account_id = :accountId AND user_id = :userId
    """)
    suspend fun delete(accountId: String, userId: String)
}
```

<Aside type="tip" title="Hint · namespace records at the schema boundary">
The composite primary key prevents two accounts from accidentally sharing a profile with the same user ID. Always include both fields in reads and deletion. A single upsert is one database operation; use a Room transaction when a business update spans multiple dependent operations. Do not use destructive migration as the default upgrade strategy for retained user data.
</Aside>

Room suspend queries perform database work through Room's execution infrastructure; `suspend` on an arbitrary function does not itself move blocking work away from the main thread. See [Room DAO guidance](https://developer.android.com/training/data-storage/room/accessing-data).

