<Aside type="tip" title="Hint · state collection and work lifetime are separate">
`collectAsStateWithLifecycle()` controls UI-state collection. It does not automatically cancel arbitrary ViewModel work. Here, `repeatOnLifecycle(STARTED)` separately cancels the awaited load when the route becomes inactive and restarts it on re-entry. Changing profile, account, or refresh revision cancels the old effect. Choose a different lifecycle threshold only when product/navigation behavior requires it.
</Aside>

Obtain the Hilt ViewModel at the navigation destination, using the Hilt/Compose API approved for the installed version, then pass it to this route. Scope it to the intended back-stack entry. When the authenticated session changes, remove the protected navigation subtree and its ViewModels; changing only a composable parameter is not full session teardown.

The host owns `Scaffold`, app bars, navigation, and safe-area/inset policy. Pass its content padding through `modifier` and avoid duplicating system-bar padding. Keep the enterprise theme around the destination. Add loading announcements, headings, error semantics, and accessibility checks appropriate to the actual design-system components.

