```kotlin
package com.enterprise.mobile.di

import com.enterprise.mobile.core.profile.EpochClock
import com.enterprise.mobile.core.profile.IoDispatcher
import com.enterprise.mobile.core.profile.MainDispatcher
import dagger.Module
import dagger.Provides
import dagger.hilt.InstallIn
import dagger.hilt.components.SingletonComponent
import javax.inject.Singleton
import kotlinx.coroutines.CoroutineDispatcher
import kotlinx.coroutines.Dispatchers

@Module
@InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class)
object ProfileInfrastructureModule {
    @Provides
    @IoDispatcher
    fun provideIoDispatcher(): CoroutineDispatcher = Dispatchers.IO

    @Provides
    @MainDispatcher
    fun provideMainDispatcher(): CoroutineDispatcher = Dispatchers.Main.immediate

    @Provides
    @Singleton
    fun provideEpochClock(): EpochClock = EpochClock { System.currentTimeMillis() }
}
```

<Aside type="tip" title="Hint · reuse existing infrastructure bindings">
Use the application's existing dispatcher qualifiers, clock, database, and network providers where available. Do not register duplicate bindings. The repository lives in the ViewModel component; that scope is not automatically an authenticated-account scope. Session ownership and replacement still belong to the application.
</Aside>

**Required host bindings:** `UserApiService`, `UserDao`, `ProfileSessionGuard`, and `ProfileDiagnostics`. Register `UserEntity` in the real Room database, enable schema export, and add migrations. Configure the application and host with the required Hilt annotations. No fallback unauthenticated client, silent diagnostics implementation, or unrestricted session guard is supplied here.

Dispatchers and clock are injected so tests can control execution and time. Avoid embedding real network or database construction in previews or composables.

